on and Culture\nFreising and Garching\nPublic holidays & festivities\nBefore departure\nWelcome @TUM-GS Event Program\nProgram and Registration\nTerms and Conditions\nEqual Opportunities\nDoing a Doctorate with Family\nFirst-Generation Academics\nInclusion\nDiversity Advising Offices\nMental Health & Wellbeing\nTUM-GS Community\nGreetings from Abroad\nWelcome to my Lab - Video Series\nLooking Behind the Doctorate\nEngage\nSupervision\nSupervisor Training\nEvents\nGlobal Perspectives\nGlobal Perspectives \u2013 India\nGlobal Perspectives - Latin America\nGlobal Perspectives \u2013 Southeast Asia\nInternationalize your Doctorate\nTUM Doctoral Day & TUMblue 2025\nTUM Doctoral Day & TUMblue 2026\nKick-Off Seminar\nHalfway There\nTowards the Finish Line\nWelcome@TUM-GS Program\nTUM Graduate School\nObjectives & Tasks\nStructure & Organization\nManagement Board\nCommittee of Graduate Center Spokespersons\nScientific Council\nQuality Management\nQuality Assurance during the Doctorate\nOrganizational Processes at TUM Graduate School\nGraduate Centers\nGraduate Council\nManagement Office\nAuftragsvergabe\nContact TUM-GS\nDirections\nDoctorate at the Technical University of Munich\nPath to a doctorate\nFunding\nThere are various options to fund your doctorate (Photo: Adobe Stock)\nFunding\nTUM does not charge any tuition fees for a doctorate. The German state bears all costs of doctoral training. Nevertheless, you will need to cover your daily expenses. There are several ways of financing your living expenses during a doctorate.\nTUM Employment Contract\nEmployment as an academic assistant is the traditional way to finance a doctorate, and offers extensive professional practice in both research and teaching. [more]\nScholarship\nA scholarship lets you finance your living expenses, and often also provides an accompanying ideational support program. [more]\nOther Funding\nEmployment with a company or a non-university institute is another option for earning money and completing 